  - var newskey = '2018-08-20-presentations-at-expressive-and-siggraph-appy-hour-2018';

//-
  block date
    | [date]

  block title
    | [title]

block newscontent
  p.card-text
  p
    | On August 15th 2018, Max Reimann and Amir Semmo presented the demo "MaeSTrO: Mobile-Style Transfer Orchestration Using Adaptive Neural Networks" at 
    a.external(href="http://s2018.siggraph.org/content/appy-hour" target="_blank" title="Öffnet externen Link im aktuellen Fenster") SIGGRAPH Appy Hour
    | , in ccoperation with the project partner Digital Masterpieces GmbH represented by Sebastian Pasewaldt. MaeSTrO is a mobile app for image stylization that empowers users to direct, edit and perform a neural style transfer with creative control. From August 17th-19th 2018 the working group also presented three contributions at the Joint Symposium on Computational Aesthetics, Sketch-Based Interfaces and Modeling, and Non-Photorealistic Animation and Rendering (
    a.external(href="http://expressive.graphics/2018" target="_blank" title="Öffnet externen Link im aktuellen Fenster") Expressive
    | )
  p SIGGRAPH 2018 was held from 12th to 16th August in Vancouver, BC, Canada. Expressive 2018 was officially co-located with SIGGRAPH 2018 and took place from 17th to 19th August in Victoria, BC, Canada.
